00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.780
Now on the model updates front, researchers introduced something called filtered reasoning score.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.500
Filtered reasoning score evaluates reasoning quality only on a model's top-k percent most

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.080
confident traces rather than averaging across all outputs. This approach differentiates models that

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.900
achieve similar benchmark accuracy but differs substantially in faithfulness, coherence,

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.900
utility, and factuality. Models with higher filtered reasoning score on one benchmark

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.520
tend to transfer better to others in both accuracy and reasoning quality.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.160
The team open sourced the evaluation code base so you can start using it immediately in your own

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:27.240
experiments. Next there is a new training method called self-distillation 0 or SD0. SD0 turns binary

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:32.640
rewards into dense token level supervision without needing an external teacher model or high-quality

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.920
demonstrations. A single model alternates between generator and reviser roles then distills the

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.720
revisers improved outputs back into the generator via on-policy self-distillation. On math and code

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:50.320
benchmarks using Quen3-4B instruct an ALMO 3-7B instruct it delivered at least 10% gains over

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:56.180
base models. It also outperformed rejection fine-tuning GRPO and self-distillation fine-tuning under

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:01.200
identical compute budgets. The method shows clear token level self-localization and iterative

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.260
self-evolution which is pretty cool to see. Then there is the cure framework for long-form

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:12.200
factuality. Cure teaches large language models to reason about uncertainty at the individual claim

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.720
level. It uses a claim-aware reasoning protocol that pairs atomic claims with explicit confidence

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:23.280
estimates. A multi-stage pipeline first aligns confidence with correctness, then optimizes for

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.380
factuality. This enables selective prediction where the model can abstain on uncertain claims

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.960
instead of hallucinating. It improved claim level accuracy by up to 39.9% on biography generation.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:41.580
It also increased AUROC by 16% on fact bench while preserving recall that is a serious jump

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.040
in trustworthy long-form generation. Shifting over to agent and tool developments,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:52.020
CROO officially launched the CROO agent protocol. This creates decentralized commercial

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:57.620
